/**
@page systemd systemd integration

ascii-chat can run under systemd on Linux. The application sends logs directly
to journald and disables terminal-only startup UI and update checks. The
packaged units discard stdout and stderr.

When systemd provides `NOTIFY_SOCKET`, the process sends `READY=1` and startup
`STATUS=` notifications. Support is optional at runtime, so the same binary
works outside systemd. Install the packaged units with
`scripts/install-systemd-confs.sh`; pass `--user` for user services and
`--uninstall` to remove them. System-wide changes require root.

@section systemd_mcp MCP HTTP server

The `ascii-chat-mcp-server.service` unit runs `ascii-chat mcp-server --transport=http`.
It serves `/mcp` on `127.0.0.1:27228` and `[::1]:27228` by default.

For a user session, install and enable the unit with:
@code{.sh}
./scripts/install-systemd-confs.sh --user
systemctl --user enable --now ascii-chat-mcp-server.service
journalctl --user -u ascii-chat-mcp-server.service -f
@endcode

For a system-wide service, install the units and enable the MCP unit with:
@code{.sh}
sudo ./scripts/install-systemd-confs.sh
sudo systemctl enable --now ascii-chat-mcp-server.service
sudo journalctl -u ascii-chat-mcp-server.service -f
@endcode

Set `ASCII_CHAT_BINARY` when running the installer to select an absolute
executable path. See @ref md_docs_2mcp for HTTP transport options.
*/
